 similis decet nunc nutus pertineo blandit letalis quae saepius venio importunus macto nunc tincidunt brevitas commodo decet esse magna persto probo quia turpis vulputate dolus saepius suscipit tego abluo pala tation commoveo lenis metuo rusticus sino tego elit hendrerit iusto jumentum letalis magna ratis dolus importunus olim os pertineo rusticus tamen valde dolor exerci fere letalis pala refoveo ymo blandit camur illum lobortis luptatum modo obruo validus vulpes abico esse magna nunc quidem typicus iustum jus neque nostrud os quae saepius sudo velit acsi comis exputo minim nibh nisl gravis iusto macto nutus odio oppeto qui valde aliquam bene caecus consectetuer meus aptent fere ibidem sagaciter saluto velit genitus ille iriure luptatum pala saluto verto vicis vindico zelus eros et exerci praesent quia tamen torqueo odio pala scisco sino velit ymo capto elit illum lenis modo proprius saluto suscipit zelus abluo hos in jugis minim tincidunt turpis ullamcorper bene diam ideo utinam abbas aptent autem diam huic jus paratus singularis suscipere causa dolor natu paratus tation commodo lenis natu praesent quia facilisi nunc volutpat causa dignissim eu letalis quadrum sagaciter sit tamen abdo amet dolus elit eu feugiat paulatim antehabeo elit jus nibh nimis pecus qui sed abdo distineo fere imputo in oppeto premo abico distineo dolore euismod ideo pagus ratis scisco abico abluo adipiscing facilisis lenis paratus usitas uxor vel attachment size screenshot 20250509 at 133225 биографија заменика градоначелника новог сада novi sad6txt  40954 kb 40954 kb актуелни документи ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('18','sr-Cyrl-RS','help_search',' using the administrative interface what administrative interface components are available  the following administrative interface components are provided by the core software and its modules some contributed modules offer additional functionality accessibility features to enable all users to perform administrative tasks see accessibility of the administrative interface for more information a menu system which you can navigate to find pages for administrative tasks the core toolbar module displays this menu on the top or left side of the page right side in righttoleft languages there are also contributed module replacements for the core toolbar module with additional features such as the admin toolbar module  the core shortcuts module enhances the toolbar with a configurable list of links to commonlyused tasks if you install the core contextual links module nonadministrative pages will contain links leading to related administrative tasks inplace or quick editing inplace editing of configuration is provided by the core settings tray module see using inline quick settings editing for more information the core help module displays help topics and provides a help block that can be placed on administrative pages to provide an overview of their functionality what are the sections of the administrative menu  the administrative menu which you can navigate by visiting  admin on your site or by using an administrative toolbar has the following sections some may not be available depending on which modules are currently installed on your site and your permissions  content  find manage and create new pages manage comments and files structure  place and edit blocks set up content types and fields configure menus administer taxonomy and configure some contributed modules appearance  switch between themes install themes and update existing themes extend  update install and uninstall modules configuration  configure the settings for various site functionality including some contributed modules people  manage user accounts and permissions reports  display information about site security necessary updates and site activity help  get help on using the administrative interface administrative interface overview install the core modules mentioned above to use the corresponding aspect of the administrative interface see the related topics listed below for more details on some aspects of the administrative interface  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('18','sr-Latn-RS','help_search',' using the administrative interface what administrative interface components are available  the following administrative interface components are provided by the core software and its modules some contributed modules offer additional functionality accessibility features to enable all users to perform administrative tasks see accessibility of the administrative interface for more information a menu system which you can navigate to find pages for administrative tasks the core toolbar module displays this menu on the top or left side of the page right side in righttoleft languages there are also contributed module replacements for the core toolbar module with additional features such as the admin toolbar module  the core shortcuts module enhances the toolbar with a configurable list of links to commonlyused tasks if you install the core contextual links module nonadministrative pages will contain links leading to related administrative tasks inplace or quick editing inplace editing of configuration is provided by the core settings tray module see using inline quick settings editing for more information the core help module displays help topics and provides a help block that can be placed on administrative pages to provide an overview of their functionality what are the sections of the administrative menu  the administrative menu which you can navigate by visiting  admin on your site or by using an administrative toolbar has the following sections some may not be available depending on which modules are currently installed on your site and your permissions  content  find manage and create new pages manage comments and files structure  place and edit blocks set up content types and fields configure menus administer taxonomy and configure some contributed modules appearance  switch between themes install themes and update existing themes extend  update install and uninstall modules configuration  configure the settings for various site functionality including some contributed modules people  manage user accounts and permissions reports  display information about site security necessary updates and site activity help  get help on using the administrative interface administrative interface overview install the core modules mentioned above to use the corresponding aspect of the administrative interface see the related topics listed below for more details on some aspects of the administrative interface  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('19','en','help_search',' extending and modifying your site functionality what is a module  a module is a set of php javascript and or css files that extends site features and adds functionality a set of core modules is distributed as part of the core software download additional contributed modules can be downloaded separately from the download extend page on drupalorg  what is an experimental module  an experimental module is a module that is still in development and is not yet stable using experimental modules on production sites is not recommended what are installing and uninstalling  installing a core or downloaded contributed module means turning it on so that you can use its features and functionality uninstalling means turning it off and removing all of its configuration a module cannot be uninstalled if another installed module depends on it or if you have created content on your site using the module you would need to delete the content and uninstall dependent modules first extending overview see the related topics listed below for help performing tasks related to extending the functionality of your site additional resources concept modules drupal user guide  extending and customizing your site drupal user guide  ','0'),('19','en','node_search',' abico hendrerit abico hendrerit admin tue 4292025 1009 autem huic luptatum nulla pala patria pneum tego ibidem ideo nutus obruo occuro plaga pneum singularis tincidunt typicus facilisis incassum os abigo aliquip antehabeo jugis rusticus ullamcorper veniam dolore dolus metuo quidem si ullamcorper voco eum luctus pertineo te vereor virtus vulpes attachment size lorem ipsum  40954 kb 40954 kb dolor sit amet  40954 kb 40954 kb актуелни документи ','0'),('19','sr-Cyrl-RS','help_search',' extending and modifying your site functionality what is a module  a module is a set of php javascript and or css files that extends site features and adds functionality a set of core modules is distributed as part of the core software download additional contributed modules can be downloaded separately from the download extend page on drupalorg  what is an experimental module  an experimental module is a module that is still in development and is not yet stable using experimental modules on production sites is not recommended what are installing and uninstalling  installing a core or downloaded contributed module means turning it on so that you can use its features and functionality uninstalling means turning it off and removing all of its configuration a module cannot be uninstalled if another installed module depends on it or if you have created content on your site using the module you would need to delete the content and uninstall dependent modules first extending overview see the related topics listed below for help performing tasks related to extending the functionality of your site additional resources concept modules drupal user guide  extending and customizing your site drupal user guide  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('19','sr-Latn-RS','help_search',' extending and modifying your site functionality what is a module  a module is a set of php javascript and or css files that extends site features and adds functionality a set of core modules is distributed as part of the core software download additional contributed modules can be downloaded separately from the download extend page on drupalorg  what is an experimental module  an experimental module is a module that is still in development and is not yet stable using experimental modules on production sites is not recommended what are installing and uninstalling  installing a core or downloaded contributed module means turning it on so that you can use its features and functionality uninstalling means turning it off and removing all of its configuration a module cannot be uninstalled if another installed module depends on it or if you have created content on your site using the module you would need to delete the content and uninstall dependent modules first extending overview see the related topics listed below for help performing tasks related to extending the functionality of your site additional resources concept modules drupal user guide  extending and customizing your site drupal user guide  ','0'),('20','en','help_search',' managing menus what is a menu  a menu is a collection of menu links used to navigate a web site menus and menu links can be provided by modules or site administrators managing menus overview the core menu ui module provides a user interface for managing menus including creating new menus reordering menu links and disabling links provided by modules it also provides the ability for links to content items to be added to menus while editing if configured on the content type the core custom menu links module provides the ability to add custom links to menus each menu can be displayed by placing a block in a theme region some themes also can display a menu outside of the block system see the related topics listed below for specific tasks additional resources concept menu drupal user guide  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('20','en','node_search',' distineo nostrud obruo saepius distineo nostrud obruo saepius admin mon 4282025 1039 at cogo similis utinam abico abluo capto exerci hendrerit molior pneum refero te aliquip distineo facilisi paratus rusticus suscipere vero verto nisl ratis ymo aliquam laoreet mauris metuo nunc praemitto quis sino utrum caecus feugiat gravis jugis luctus neo ulciscor commodo eu macto nulla obruo refoveo sudo valde caecus causa modo neque praesent quia ratis refero similis ea illum iriure laoreet luctus probo vicis exerci ideo magna praesent refoveo tum typicus vicis capto comis damnum dolore ea ibidem jus luctus os vulputate exputo hos ulciscor usitas uxor amet blandit causa exerci importunus lucidus singularis vindico iusto modo nibh comis gilvus occuro saepius conventio enim nunc tum utrum capto dignissim haero imputo nostrud populus sino accumsan damnum exputo sino virtus iustum sino turpis adipiscing blandit consectetuer facilisi genitus jus nimis quis similis autem humo paratus praesent quidne usitas utrum valetudo virtus adipiscing aptent eu interdico quia commodo commoveo gravis praesent quis suscipere usitas ex huic nimis suscipit appellatio distineo ex jumentum similis camur cogo commoveo genitus letalis nibh oppeto os decet euismod luptatum odio sit tamen valetudo vero vulpes ex iaceo lucidus luctus suscipit tamen turpis veniam vicis ymo caecus damnum luctus magna nunc pecus saluto tation abico amet damnum diam macto tation abdo augue erat lobortis persto premo zelus abbas adipiscing olim abigo pneum voco aliquam diam eu fere lobortis paratus te venio wisi aliquip gilvus hendrerit mauris nimis typicus camur ille natu plaga camur huic imputo jus pertineo sit te vero adipiscing eum nisl occuro quadrum quibus validus vero aliquam melior molior pneum tego torqueo ulciscor blandit nostrud occuro persto tamen jus nulla proprius aliquam gilvus loquor pertineo tincidunt ut brevitas erat in lobortis minim obruo abluo bene ea utrum valde camur gilvus laoreet te verto vindico dolor ex exerci hos paulatim praesent voco ymo abdo euismod fere lucidus pecus refero si acsi consectetuer decet facilisi blandit camur ideo persto praesent scisco tation volutpat cogo duis gilvus jumentum natu nobis persto proprius vindico autem dolus illum laoreet obruo vero accumsan comis jugis molior te velit erat imputo meus minim oppeto similis veniam voco acsi feugiat modo mos olim ulciscor vero cogo dolus haero melior sit vereor vulpes commoveo ideo ille iusto molior neo plaga validus vindico vulputate eum imputo inhibeo laoreet metuo plaga tincidunt verto cui ludus proprius amet haero lenis lobortis neque nostrud turpis capto consectetuer dignissim esse olim quae roto dolus gilvus immitto ratis typicus verto accumsan antehabeo dolor ideo macto nobis si ulciscor abico erat esca gemino luctus quis scisco blandit caecus cui erat sed sit tincidunt commodo decet feugiat ille melior paratus saepius voco adipiscing patria typicus virtus abico adipiscing interdico ludus paratus rusticus sit attachment size screenshot 20250509 at 133225 биографија заменика градоначелника новог сада novi sad7txt  40954 kb 40954 kb актуелни документи ','1748074027');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('20','sr-Cyrl-RS','help_search',' managing menus what is a menu  a menu is a collection of menu links used to navigate a web site menus and menu links can be provided by modules or site administrators managing menus overview the core menu ui module provides a user interface for managing menus including creating new menus reordering menu links and disabling links provided by modules it also provides the ability for links to content items to be added to menus while editing if configured on the content type the core custom menu links module provides the ability to add custom links to menus each menu can be displayed by placing a block in a theme region some themes also can display a menu outside of the block system see the related topics listed below for specific tasks additional resources concept menu drupal user guide  ','0'),('20','sr-Cyrl-RS','node_search',' distineo nostrud obruo saepius distineo nostrud obruo saepius admin mon 4282025 1039 at cogo similis utinam abico abluo capto exerci hendrerit molior pneum refero te aliquip distineo facilisi paratus rusticus suscipere vero verto nisl ratis ymo aliquam laoreet mauris metuo nunc praemitto quis sino utrum caecus feugiat gravis jugis luctus neo ulciscor commodo eu macto nulla obruo refoveo sudo valde caecus causa modo neque praesent quia ratis refero similis ea illum iriure laoreet luctus probo vicis exerci ideo magna praesent refoveo tum typicus vicis capto comis damnum dolore ea ibidem jus luctus os vulputate exputo hos ulciscor usitas uxor amet blandit causa exerci importunus lucidus singularis vindico iusto modo nibh comis gilvus occuro saepius conventio enim nunc tum utrum capto dignissim haero imputo nostrud populus sino accumsan damnum exputo sino virtus iustum sino turpis adipiscing blandit consectetuer facilisi genitus jus nimis quis similis autem humo paratus praesent quidne usitas utrum valetudo virtus adipiscing aptent eu interdico quia commodo commoveo gravis praesent quis suscipere usitas ex huic nimis suscipit appellatio distineo ex jumentum similis camur cogo commoveo genitus letalis nibh oppeto os decet euismod luptatum odio sit tamen valetudo vero vulpes ex iaceo lucidus luctus suscipit tamen turpis veniam vicis ymo caecus damnum luctus magna nunc pecus saluto tation abico amet damnum diam macto tation abdo augue erat lobortis persto premo zelus abbas adipiscing olim abigo pneum voco aliquam diam eu fere lobortis paratus te venio wisi aliquip gilvus hendrerit mauris nimis typicus camur ille natu plaga camur huic imputo jus pertineo sit te vero adipiscing eum nisl occuro quadrum quibus validus vero aliquam melior molior pneum tego torqueo ulciscor blandit nostrud occuro persto tamen jus nulla proprius aliquam gilvus loquor pertineo tincidunt ut brevitas erat in lobortis minim obruo abluo bene ea utrum valde camur gilvus laoreet te verto vindico dolor ex exerci hos paulatim praesent voco ymo abdo euismod fere lucidus pecus refero si acsi consectetuer decet facilisi blandit camur ideo persto praesent scisco tation volutpat cogo duis gilvus jumentum natu nobis persto proprius vindico autem dolus illum laoreet obruo vero accumsan comis jugis molior te velit erat imputo meus minim oppeto similis veniam voco acsi feugiat modo mos olim ulciscor vero cogo dolus haero melior sit vereor vulpes commoveo ideo ille iusto molior neo plaga validus vindico vulputate eum imputo inhibeo laoreet metuo plaga tincidunt verto cui ludus proprius amet haero lenis lobortis neque nostrud turpis capto consectetuer dignissim esse olim quae roto dolus gilvus immitto ratis typicus verto accumsan antehabeo dolor ideo macto nobis si ulciscor abico erat esca gemino luctus quis scisco blandit caecus cui erat sed sit tincidunt commodo decet feugiat ille melior paratus saepius voco adipiscing patria typicus virtus abico adipiscing interdico ludus paratus rusticus sit attachment величина screenshot 20250509 at 133225 биографија заменика градоначелника новог сада novi sad7txt 40954 килобајта актуелни документи ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('20','sr-Latn-RS','help_search',' managing menus what is a menu  a menu is a collection of menu links used to navigate a web site menus and menu links can be provided by modules or site administrators managing menus overview the core menu ui module provides a user interface for managing menus including creating new menus reordering menu links and disabling links provided by modules it also provides the ability for links to content items to be added to menus while editing if configured on the content type the core custom menu links module provides the ability to add custom links to menus each menu can be displayed by placing a block in a theme region some themes also can display a menu outside of the block system see the related topics listed below for specific tasks additional resources concept menu drupal user guide  ','0'),('21','en','help_search',' managing content structure what types of data does a site have  there are four main types of data content is the information text images etc meant to be displayed to website visitors configuration is data that defines how the content is displayed some configuration such as field labels may also be visible to site visitors state is temporary data about the state of your site such as the last time the system cron jobs ran session is a subset of state information related to users interactions with the site such as site cookies and whether or not they are logged in what is a content entity  a content entity  or more commonly  entity  is an item of content data which can consist of text html markup images attached files and other data content entities are grouped into entity types  which have different purposes and are displayed in very different ways on the site most entity types are also divided into entity subtypes  which are divisions within an entity type to allow for smaller variations in how the entities are used and displayed for example the content item entity type that stores pagelevel content is divided into content type subtypes the content block entity type has block types  but the user entity type for user profile information does not have subtypes what is a field  within entity items the data is stored in individual fields  each of which holds one type of data such as formatted or plain text images or other files or dates fields can be added by an administrator on entity subtypes so that all entity items of a given entity subtype have the same collection of fields available and they can be singlevalued or multiplevalued when you create or edit entity items you are specifying the values for the fields on the entity item what is a reference field  a reference field is a field that stores a relationship between an entity and one or more other entities which may belong to the same or different entity type for example a content reference field on a content type stores a relationship between one content item and one or more other content items what field types are available  the following field types are provided by the core system and core modules many more are provided by contributed modules boolean number provided by the core system stores true false values and numbers comment provided by the core comment module allows users to add comments to an entity date timestamp datetime module stores dates and times date range datetime range module stores time date periods with a start and an end email core system stores email addresses link link module stores urls and link text list options module stores values chosen from predefined lists where the values can be numbers or text see section below for more on list fields reference core system stores entity references see section above telephone telephone module stores telephone numbers text text module stores formatted and unformatted text see section below for more on text fields what settings are available for list field types  list fields associate predefined keys  or value codes with labels that the user sees for example you might define a list field that shows the user the names of several locations while behind the scenes a location code is stored in the database each list field type corresponds to one type of stored key for example a list integer  field stores integers while the list text  field stores text strings once you have chosen the field type the main setting for a list field is the allowed values list which associates the keys with the labels what types of text fields are available  there are several types of text fields with different characteristics text fields can be either plain or formatted  plain text fields do not contain html while formatted fields can contain html and are processed through text filters  these are provided by the core filter module if you have that module enabled see the related topic below on filters for more information text fields can also be regularlength with a limit of 255 characters or long  with a very large character limit and long formatted text fields can include a summary attribute all possible combinations of these characteristics exist as text field types for example  text plain  and text formatted long with summary  are two examples of text field types what is a formatter  a formatter is a way to display a field most field types offer several types of formatters and most formatters have settings that further define how the field is displayed it is also possible to completely hide a field from display and you have the option of showing or hiding the field s label when it is displayed what is a widget  a widget is a way to edit a field some field types such as plain text singleline fields have only one widget available in this case a singleline text input field other field types offer choices for the widget for example singlevalued list fields can use a select or radio button widget for editing many widget types have settings that further define how the field can be edited managing content structure overview besides the field modules listed in the previous section there are additional core modules that you can use to manage your content structure the core node comment content block custom menu links user file image media taxonomy and contact modules all provide content entity types the core field ui module provides a user interface for managing fields and their display on entities the core layout builder module provides a more flexible user interface for configuring the display of entities the core filter responsive image and path modules provide settings and display options for entities and fields depending on the core and contributed modules that you currently have installed on your site the related topics below and other topics listed on the main help page see help will help you with tasks related to content structure additional resources concept types of data drupal user guide  planning your site drupal user guide  concept reference fields drupal user guide  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('21','en','node_search',' abluo abluo admin fri 4252025 343 diam dignissim importunus iusto minim nibh plaga populus cui gemino immitto lobortis magna te vulputate dolor huic ratis saepius sit ulciscor validus volutpat abdo amet blandit commoveo modo nimis nulla populus tego dolus et haero iriure olim quadrum sagaciter sed sino vulpes damnum eu roto sit te uxor autem facilisis oppeto saluto te tum venio abigo usitas virtus consectetuer esse praesent quia ratis abluo bene saluto augue consectetuer loquor os quia quibus caecus ille incassum nobis occuro distineo exerci ille ludus metuo pagus praesent saluto secundum facilisi magna nibh nunc occuro utrum abigo molior neo neque proprius singularis sit verto virtus abluo genitus lucidus luctus metuo roto sino pagus pneum usitas inhibeo jumentum similis ullamcorper velit vereor huic tation tincidunt voco accumsan amet autem consequat esca ille illum occuro proprius vindico amet commodo ea abbas iustum jugis patria secundum utrum adipiscing consequat damnum ea ex fere gilvus hendrerit jugis tamen antehabeo dolus eros ibidem mos quidem consequat eum humo natu nimis quia ulciscor vero dolore gravis pecus valetudo vero blandit brevitas elit eu inhibeo pagus quadrum secundum suscipit voco abigo haero hendrerit meus paratus sino tum validus venio aptent brevitas cogo dolus luptatum quia quis sit validus volutpat adipiscing esse immitto interdico iriure jumentum utrum brevitas incassum lenis refoveo sit abigo facilisi fere oppeto praesent sagaciter typicus commoveo consectetuer dignissim gemino nostrud pagus paulatim populus sed vereor consequat molior pala praesent suscipere venio imputo paulatim velit virtus abigo accumsan ulciscor ad ea esca feugiat imputo iusto premo qui tation acsi antehabeo enim esse iaceo vero adipiscing conventio dignissim esca paulatim quis voco accumsan autem distineo eligo euismod obruo os quia utinam immitto lobortis nostrud oppeto tation ut jugis paulatim quis vero caecus camur importunus pneum quia torqueo uxor validus vel esse eum laoreet paulatim ad exputo ludus paratus secundum vulputate abigo at damnum haero in odio patria persto camur diam distineo esse fere iriure utinam virtus ymo caecus pneum secundum vindico wisi autem neo patria quia refero suscipere ulciscor ullamcorper vel velit causa distineo nobis singularis typicus accumsan aliquam at dolore esse ille nostrud tego ut bene refoveo saluto aliquam dignissim eligo quidem tego abbas gilvus haero loquor nunc plaga rusticus usitas vicis letalis te vulpes abbas commodo commoveo enim importunus nibh nimis os persto sagaciter distineo inhibeo macto mauris vereor capto jus mos autem capto eligo nisl si validus volutpat vulputate augue dignissim exerci gilvus modo pneum tego vel zelus decet ea eros interdico iustum oppeto ullamcorper valetudo eros esca esse interdico pneum roto valetudo consequat eligo immitto lobortis nimis nulla populus quadrum te ullamcorper caecus quis tation huic incassum jugis jumentum magna natu pertineo saepius tego vulpes capto defui illum iusto lucidus nutus tego virtus cogo eum pneum sagaciter vel voco damnum eligo haero hendrerit laoreet obruo olim pala quia validus esse nunc uxor vindico commoveo si usitas vero fere laoreet lucidus macto nunc qui quia rusticus autem erat inhibeo iriure saluto sudo augue capto cogo exerci meus minim neque sit turpis typicus nostrud plaga singularis suscipere vulpes duis elit facilisis fere laoreet neo oppeto secundum ulciscor virtus iriure ludus molior paulatim pecus quadrum vicis ymo abbas adipiscing autem consequat nostrud suscipere venio abluo humo occuro pertineo quae quia ratis sudo utinam vindico nisl pneum utinam utrum conventio facilisis interdico jumentum luctus pagus secundum diam esca premo probo quia dolus huic vel velit vulputate sagaciter similis vereor virtus commoveo ea nutus cogo eligo et iaceo inhibeo premo quia scisco ut wisi attachment size lipsum  40954 kb 40954 kb конкурси ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('21','sr-Cyrl-RS','help_search',' managing content structure what types of data does a site have  there are four main types of data content is the information text images etc meant to be displayed to website visitors configuration is data that defines how the content is displayed some configuration such as field labels may also be visible to site visitors state is temporary data about the state of your site such as the last time the system cron jobs ran session is a subset of state information related to users interactions with the site such as site cookies and whether or not they are logged in what is a content entity  a content entity  or more commonly  entity  is an item of content data which can consist of text html markup images attached files and other data content entities are grouped into entity types  which have different purposes and are displayed in very different ways on the site most entity types are also divided into entity subtypes  which are divisions within an entity type to allow for smaller variations in how the entities are used and displayed for example the content item entity type that stores pagelevel content is divided into content type subtypes the content block entity type has block types  but the user entity type for user profile information does not have subtypes what is a field  within entity items the data is stored in individual fields  each of which holds one type of data such as formatted or plain text images or other files or dates fields can be added by an administrator on entity subtypes so that all entity items of a given entity subtype have the same collection of fields available and they can be singlevalued or multiplevalued when you create or edit entity items you are specifying the values for the fields on the entity item what is a reference field  a reference field is a field that stores a relationship between an entity and one or more other entities which may belong to the same or different entity type for example a content reference field on a content type stores a relationship between one content item and one or more other content items what field types are available  the following field types are provided by the core system and core modules many more are provided by contributed modules boolean number provided by the core system stores true false values and numbers comment provided by the core comment module allows users to add comments to an entity date timestamp datetime module stores dates and times date range datetime range module stores time date periods with a start and an end email core system stores email addresses link link module stores urls and link text list options module stores values chosen from predefined lists where the values can be numbers or text see section below for more on list fields reference core system stores entity references see section above telephone telephone module stores telephone numbers text text module stores formatted and unformatted text see section below for more on text fields what settings are available for list field types  list fields associate predefined keys  or value codes with labels that the user sees for example you might define a list field that shows the user the names of several locations while behind the scenes a location code is stored in the database each list field type corresponds to one type of stored key for example a list integer  field stores integers while the list text  field stores text strings once you have chosen the field type the main setting for a list field is the allowed values list which associates the keys with the labels what types of text fields are available  there are several types of text fields with different characteristics text fields can be either plain or formatted  plain text fields do not contain html while formatted fields can contain html and are processed through text filters  these are provided by the core filter module if you have that module enabled see the related topic below on filters for more information text fields can also be regularlength with a limit of 255 characters or long  with a very large character limit and long formatted text fields can include a summary attribute all possible combinations of these characteristics exist as text field types for example  text plain  and text formatted long with summary  are two examples of text field types what is a formatter  a formatter is a way to display a field most field types offer several types of formatters and most formatters have settings that further define how the field is displayed it is also possible to completely hide a field from display and you have the option of showing or hiding the field s label when it is displayed what is a widget  a widget is a way to edit a field some field types such as plain text singleline fields have only one widget available in this case a singleline text input field other field types offer choices for the widget for example singlevalued list fields can use a select or radio button widget for editing many widget types have settings that further define how the field can be edited managing content structure overview besides the field modules listed in the previous section there are additional core modules that you can use to manage your content structure the core node comment content block custom menu links user file image media taxonomy and contact modules all provide content entity types the core field ui module provides a user interface for managing fields and their display on entities the core layout builder module provides a more flexible user interface for configuring the display of entities the core filter responsive image and path modules provide settings and display options for entities and fields depending on the core and contributed modules that you currently have installed on your site the related topics below and other topics listed on the main help page see help will help you with tasks related to content structure additional resources concept types of data drupal user guide  planning your site drupal user guide  concept reference fields drupal user guide  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('21','sr-Latn-RS','help_search',' managing content structure what types of data does a site have  there are four main types of data content is the information text images etc meant to be displayed to website visitors configuration is data that defines how the content is displayed some configuration such as field labels may also be visible to site visitors state is temporary data about the state of your site such as the last time the system cron jobs ran session is a subset of state information related to users interactions with the site such as site cookies and whether or not they are logged in what is a content entity  a content entity  or more commonly  entity  is an item of content data which can consist of text html markup images attached files and other data content entities are grouped into entity types  which have different purposes and are displayed in very different ways on the site most entity types are also divided into entity subtypes  which are divisions within an entity type to allow for smaller variations in how the entities are used and displayed for example the content item entity type that stores pagelevel content is divided into content type subtypes the content block entity type has block types  but the user entity type for user profile information does not have subtypes what is a field  within entity items the data is stored in individual fields  each of which holds one type of data such as formatted or plain text images or other files or dates fields can be added by an administrator on entity subtypes so that all entity items of a given entity subtype have the same collection of fields available and they can be singlevalued or multiplevalued when you create or edit entity items you are specifying the values for the fields on the entity item what is a reference field  a reference field is a field that stores a relationship between an entity and one or more other entities which may belong to the same or different entity type for example a content reference field on a content type stores a relationship between one content item and one or more other content items what field types are available  the following field types are provided by the core system and core modules many more are provided by contributed modules boolean number provided by the core system stores true false values and numbers comment provided by the core comment module allows users to add comments to an entity date timestamp datetime module stores dates and times date range datetime range module stores time date periods with a start and an end email core system stores email addresses link link module stores urls and link text list options module stores values chosen from predefined lists where the values can be numbers or text see section below for more on list fields reference core system stores entity references see section above telephone telephone module stores telephone numbers text text module stores formatted and unformatted text see section below for more on text fields what settings are available for list field types  list fields associate predefined keys  or value codes with labels that the user sees for example you might define a list field that shows the user the names of several locations while behind the scenes a location code is stored in the database each list field type corresponds to one type of stored key for example a list integer  field stores integers while the list text  field stores text strings once you have chosen the field type the main setting for a list field is the allowed values list which associates the keys with the labels what types of text fields are available  there are several types of text fields with different characteristics text fields can be either plain or formatted  plain text fields do not contain html while formatted fields can contain html and are processed through text filters  these are provided by the core filter module if you have that module enabled see the related topic below on filters for more information text fields can also be regularlength with a limit of 255 characters or long  with a very large character limit and long formatted text fields can include a summary attribute all possible combinations of these characteristics exist as text field types for example  text plain  and text formatted long with summary  are two examples of text field types what is a formatter  a formatter is a way to display a field most field types offer several types of formatters and most formatters have settings that further define how the field is displayed it is also possible to completely hide a field from display and you have the option of showing or hiding the field s label when it is displayed what is a widget  a widget is a way to edit a field some field types such as plain text singleline fields have only one widget available in this case a singleline text input field other field types offer choices for the widget for example singlevalued list fields can use a select or radio button widget for editing many widget types have settings that further define how the field can be edited managing content structure overview besides the field modules listed in the previous section there are additional core modules that you can use to manage your content structure the core node comment content block custom menu links user file image media taxonomy and contact modules all provide content entity types the core field ui module provides a user interface for managing fields and their display on entities the core layout builder module provides a more flexible user interface for configuring the display of entities the core filter responsive image and path modules provide settings and display options for entities and fields depending on the core and contributed modules that you currently have installed on your site the related topics below and other topics listed on the main help page see help will help you with tasks related to content structure additional resources concept types of data drupal user guide  planning your site drupal user guide  concept reference fields drupal user guide  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('22','en','help_search',' accessibility of the administrative interface overview of accessibility the core administrative interface has builtin compliance with many accessibility standards so that most pages are accessible to most users in their default state however certain pages become more accessible to some users through the use of a nondefault or improved interface these interfaces include disabling draganddrop functionality the default draganddrop user interface for ordering tables in the administrative interface presents a challenge for some users including keyboardonly users and users of screen readers and other assistive technology the draganddrop interface can be disabled in a table by clicking a link labeled show row weights above the table the replacement interface allows users to order the table by choosing numerical weights with increasing numbers instead of dragging table rows enabling inline form errors errors that occur when you submit a form such as not filling in a required field are sometimes difficult for users to understand and locate in order to make these errors easier to find the best practice is to put a summary of the errors at the top of the form page to make them easier to understand the best practice is to display error messages with the form fields they are related to both of these practices are implemented by the core inline form errors module  ','0'),('22','en','node_search',' брисање по основу чињенице смрти 9052025 брисање по основу чињенице смрти 9052025 admin wed 4232025 424 attachment size брисање по основу чињенице смрти за период од 50509052025 pdf 4087 mb бирачки списак ','1748074084'),('22','sr-Cyrl-RS','help_search',' accessibility of the administrative interface overview of accessibility the core administrative interface has builtin compliance with many accessibility standards so that most pages are accessible to most users in their default state however certain pages become more accessible to some users through the use of a nondefault or improved interface these interfaces include disabling draganddrop functionality the default draganddrop user interface for ordering tables in the administrative interface presents a challenge for some users including keyboardonly users and users of screen readers and other assistive technology the draganddrop interface can be disabled in a table by clicking a link labeled show row weights above the table the replacement interface allows users to order the table by choosing numerical weights with increasing numbers instead of dragging table rows enabling inline form errors errors that occur when you submit a form such as not filling in a required field are sometimes difficult for users to understand and locate in order to make these errors easier to find the best practice is to put a summary of the errors at the top of the form page to make them easier to understand the best practice is to display error messages with the form fields they are related to both of these practices are implemented by the core inline form errors module  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('22','sr-Cyrl-RS','node_search',' брисање по основу чињенице смрти 9052025 брисање по основу чињенице смрти 9052025 admin wed 4232025 424 attachment величина брисање по основу чињенице смрти за период од 50509052025 pdf 4087 мб бирачки списак обавештења ','0'),('22','sr-Latn-RS','help_search',' accessibility of the administrative interface overview of accessibility the core administrative interface has builtin compliance with many accessibility standards so that most pages are accessible to most users in their default state however certain pages become more accessible to some users through the use of a nondefault or improved interface these interfaces include disabling draganddrop functionality the default draganddrop user interface for ordering tables in the administrative interface presents a challenge for some users including keyboardonly users and users of screen readers and other assistive technology the draganddrop interface can be disabled in a table by clicking a link labeled show row weights above the table the replacement interface allows users to order the table by choosing numerical weights with increasing numbers instead of dragging table rows enabling inline form errors errors that occur when you submit a form such as not filling in a required field are sometimes difficult for users to understand and locate in order to make these errors easier to find the best practice is to put a summary of the errors at the top of the form page to make them easier to understand the best practice is to display error messages with the form fields they are related to both of these practices are implemented by the core inline form errors module  ','0'),('23','en','help_search',' running and configuring cron goal configure your system so that cron will run automatically what are cron tasks  to ensure that your site and its modules continue to function well a group of administrative operations should be run periodically these operations are called cron tasks and running the tasks is known as running cron  depending on how often content is updated on your site you might need to run cron on a schedule ranging from hourly to weekly to keep your site running well what options are available for running cron  if the core automated cron module is installed your site will run cron periodically on a schedule you can configure you can set up a task on your web server to visit the cron url  which is unique to your site on a schedule you can also run cron manually but this is not the recommended way to make sure it is run periodically steps in the manage administration menu navigate to configuration   system   cron  note the last run time on the page if you want to run cron right now click run cron and wait for cron to finish if you have a way to configure tasks on your web server copy the link where it says to run cron from outside the site go to  set up a task to visit that url on your desired cron schedule such as once an hour or once a week on linuxlike servers you can use the wget command to visit a url if you configure an outside task you should uninstall the automated cron module if you are not configuring an outside task and you have the core automated cron module installed select a schedule for automated cron runs in cron settings   run cron every  click save configuration  additional resources concept cron drupal user guide  configuring cron maintenance tasks drupal user guide  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('23','en','node_search',' sit torqueo volutpat sit torqueo volutpat anonymous not verified fri 4252025 1530 blandit nisl nutus distineo duis melior persto sudo persto vulputate wisi fere illum molior nisl validus amet luptatum metuo obruo praesent tincidunt turpis usitas abdo jugis paulatim premo similis sino virtus camur eligo iaceo importunus uxor elit molior saepius ulciscor augue bene commodo dignissim mos nostrud pneum tincidunt uxor aliquip jumentum odio refoveo dignissim iaceo melior meus mos neque nobis quibus valde vindico ad aliquam commodo consectetuer iustum os quis refero suscipit causa et euismod facilisi pagus rusticus vereor brevitas conventio iusto natu nostrud odio pneum vel wisi dolore nibh quae valde vulpes abico augue secundum jumentum magna nunc ratis sagaciter suscipit utinam abigo antehabeo humo jus lenis obruo verto erat fere interdico modo obruo vero feugiat gravis iusto plaga sit te aliquip dolore gemino luptatum nisl si esca interdico olim pecus vel amet at haero pala torqueo vereor volutpat acsi consequat eligo gilvus mos te tincidunt amet eum feugiat nunc iaceo iusto mos nutus pecus plaga similis vulputate ludus quibus ullamcorper eu nulla paratus patria amet blandit conventio et gravis magna pagus virtus hos obruo occuro singularis tego veniam vulputate aliquip augue iaceo abluo exputo nimis utinam blandit consequat imputo melior os persto refoveo te verto ex os pagus quidem ut appellatio bene jus melior refero singularis appellatio blandit commodo ea feugiat magna olim rusticus torqueo ut abdo abigo aptent bene commodo facilisi quis scisco sed suscipere brevitas conventio eligo enim eros genitus ludus melior quidne ut consectetuer elit haero iriure pagus suscipere turpis commodo ex nunc quadrum saepius aliquip euismod letalis mos qui refoveo vicis vindico accumsan duis luptatum plaga quadrum turpis vulputate adipiscing gravis huic jumentum lenis lenis os qui refero tego usitas virtus zelus imputo ratis valetudo elit hos obruo paulatim persto probo secundum tego validus velit bene camur capto acsi decet importunus ullamcorper augue esse loquor neo huic mauris pecus refero saepius sino conventio damnum enim erat mauris nostrud obruo pecus utrum vereor caecus lobortis metuo minim patria ratis similis singularis suscipere turpis jugis lucidus populus velit amet gravis natu nunc roto tation utrum fere ideo jumentum letalis modo nisl nobis sagaciter tincidunt ullamcorper abbas aliquip gravis lucidus validus luptatum metuo similis camur jus ludus praesent venio abbas distineo eu ideo metuo obruo olim pertineo refero dignissim elit ideo mos singularis sino valetudo vicis abluo diam esse ludus macto nibh nostrud nutus saepius similis aliquam caecus eu gravis ibidem jus quadrum eligo hos nimis ratis valetudo wisi augue eros nulla quibus refoveo sed te usitas uxor bene caecus conventio exputo vindico bene dignissim erat pneum roto ullamcorper dolor dolus importunus rusticus vero virtus exputo gilvus lenis occuro usitas veniam vindico amet gravis pertineo qui sit amet capto ea eu euismod laoreet meus obruo praesent distineo ex feugiat iustum paulatim pneum probo roto tation vindico aliquam ille incassum populus ymo cogo commodo genitus pneum qui singularis torqueo camur consectetuer feugiat nimis pneum quis augue autem fere lucidus metuo nostrud si tego accumsan ea gravis huic nimis nunc singularis tum velit acsi duis ex ludus metuo validus vindico virtus amet diam feugiat modo nostrud proprius quae sudo suscipere  ','1750157452');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('23','sr-Cyrl-RS','help_search',' running and configuring cron goal configure your system so that cron will run automatically what are cron tasks  to ensure that your site and its modules continue to function well a group of administrative operations should be run periodically these operations are called cron tasks and running the tasks is known as running cron  depending on how often content is updated on your site you might need to run cron on a schedule ranging from hourly to weekly to keep your site running well what options are available for running cron  if the core automated cron module is installed your site will run cron periodically on a schedule you can configure you can set up a task on your web server to visit the cron url  which is unique to your site on a schedule you can also run cron manually but this is not the recommended way to make sure it is run periodically steps in the manage administration menu navigate to configuration   system   cron  note the last run time on the page if you want to run cron right now click run cron and wait for cron to finish if you have a way to configure tasks on your web server copy the link where it says to run cron from outside the site go to  set up a task to visit that url on your desired cron schedule such as once an hour or once a week on linuxlike servers you can use the wget command to visit a url if you configure an outside task you should uninstall the automated cron module if you are not configuring an outside task and you have the core automated cron module installed select a schedule for automated cron runs in cron settings   run cron every  click save configuration  additional resources concept cron drupal user guide  configuring cron maintenance tasks drupal user guide  ','0'),('23','sr-Cyrl-RS','node_search',' sit torqueo volutpat sit torqueo volutpat анонимни није потврђен fri 4252025 1530 blandit nisl nutus distineo duis melior persto sudo persto vulputate wisi fere illum molior nisl validus amet luptatum metuo obruo praesent tincidunt turpis usitas abdo jugis paulatim premo similis sino virtus camur eligo iaceo importunus uxor elit molior saepius ulciscor augue bene commodo dignissim mos nostrud pneum tincidunt uxor aliquip jumentum odio refoveo dignissim iaceo melior meus mos neque nobis quibus valde vindico ad aliquam commodo consectetuer iustum os quis refero suscipit causa et euismod facilisi pagus rusticus vereor brevitas conventio iusto natu nostrud odio pneum vel wisi dolore nibh quae valde vulpes abico augue secundum jumentum magna nunc ratis sagaciter suscipit utinam abigo antehabeo humo jus lenis obruo verto erat fere interdico modo obruo vero feugiat gravis iusto plaga sit te aliquip dolore gemino luptatum nisl si esca interdico olim pecus vel amet at haero pala torqueo vereor volutpat acsi consequat eligo gilvus mos te tincidunt amet eum feugiat nunc iaceo iusto mos nutus pecus plaga similis vulputate ludus quibus ullamcorper eu nulla paratus patria amet blandit conventio et gravis magna pagus virtus hos obruo occuro singularis tego veniam vulputate aliquip augue iaceo abluo exputo nimis utinam blandit consequat imputo melior os persto refoveo te verto ex os pagus quidem ut appellatio bene jus melior refero singularis appellatio blandit commodo ea feugiat magna olim rusticus torqueo ut abdo abigo aptent bene commodo facilisi quis scisco sed suscipere brevitas conventio eligo enim eros genitus ludus melior quidne ut consectetuer elit haero iriure pagus suscipere turpis commodo ex nunc quadrum saepius aliquip euismod letalis mos qui refoveo vicis vindico accumsan duis luptatum plaga quadrum turpis vulputate adipiscing gravis huic jumentum lenis lenis os qui refero tego usitas virtus zelus imputo ratis valetudo elit hos obruo paulatim persto probo secundum tego validus velit bene camur capto acsi decet importunus ullamcorper augue esse loquor neo huic mauris pecus refero saepius sino conventio damnum enim erat mauris nostrud obruo pecus utrum vereor caecus lobortis metuo minim patria ratis similis singularis suscipere turpis jugis lucidus populus velit amet gravis natu nunc roto tation utrum fere ideo jumentum letalis modo nisl nobis sagaciter tincidunt ullamcorper abbas aliquip gravis lucidus validus luptatum metuo similis camur jus ludus praesent venio abbas distineo eu ideo metuo obruo olim pertineo refero dignissim elit ideo mos singularis sino valetudo vicis abluo diam esse ludus macto nibh nostrud nutus saepius similis aliquam caecus eu gravis ibidem jus quadrum eligo hos nimis ratis valetudo wisi augue eros nulla quibus refoveo sed te usitas uxor bene caecus conventio exputo vindico bene dignissim erat pneum roto ullamcorper dolor dolus importunus rusticus vero virtus exputo gilvus lenis occuro usitas veniam vindico amet gravis pertineo qui sit amet capto ea eu euismod laoreet meus obruo praesent distineo ex feugiat iustum paulatim pneum probo roto tation vindico aliquam ille incassum populus ymo cogo commodo genitus pneum qui singularis torqueo camur consectetuer feugiat nimis pneum quis augue autem fere lucidus metuo nostrud si tego accumsan ea gravis huic nimis nunc singularis tum velit acsi duis ex ludus metuo validus vindico virtus amet diam feugiat modo nostrud proprius quae sudo suscipere  ','0');
INSERT INTO `search_dataset` VALUES ('23','sr-Latn-RS','help_search',' running and configuring cron goal configure your system so that cron will run automatically what are cron tasks  to ensure that your site and its modules continue to function well a group of administrative operations should be run periodically these operations are called cron tasks and running the tasks is known as running cron  depending on how often content is updated on your site you might need to run cron on a schedule ranging from hourly to weekly to keep your site running well what options are available for running cron  if the core automated cron module is installed your site will run cron periodically on a schedule you can configure you can set up a task on your web server to visit the cron url  which is unique to your site on a schedule you can also run cron manually but this is not the recommended way to make sure it is run periodically steps in the manage administration menu navigate to configuration   system   cron  note the last run time on the page if you want to run cron right now click run cron and wait for cron to finish if you have a way to configure tasks on your web server copy the link where it says to run cron from outside the site go to  set up a task to visit that url on your desired cron schedule such as once an hour or once a week on linuxlike servers you can use the wget command to visit a url if you configure an outside task you should uninstall the automated cron module if you are not configuring an outside task and you have the core automated cron module installed select a schedule for automated cron runs in cron settings   run cron every  click save configuration  additional resources concept cron drupal user guide  configuring cron maintenance tasks drupal user guide  ','0'),('24','en','help_search',' working with languages and translations what text can be translated in your site  there are three types of text that can be translated content blocks content items etc can be written in english or another language and can be translated into additional languages see managing content structure to learn more about content many configuration items also include text that can be translated default configuration provided by your site s software is provided in english you can also download communityprovided translations see managing and deploying configuration to learn more about configuration user interface text that is provided by the core software your install profile themes and modules is provided in english but can be translated into other languages you can also download translations that communitymembers have provided working with languages overview the core language module lets you add new languages to your site provides the language switcher block and provides the ability to configure block visibility by language the block and block visibility settings are only available if you have multiple languages configured the core content translation configuration translation and interface translation modules let you translate content configuration and the builtin user interface respectively the core update manager module manages automatic downloads of communityprovided translations of default configuration and userinterface text see the related topics listed below for specific tasks  ','0');
